Subject: ios: place the frame-breakdown begin/end pairs in the engine's frame

Where the time goes, in nine rows, all of them PD_IOS_PROFILER-guarded so that
every other platform (and our own oracle) is byte for byte upstream's. Patch
0026 is the build switch; app/gfx/pd_frame_prof.c is the instrument.

The engine's frame, and the row each part is counted in:

  schedStartFrame()                      the frame boundary: roll the rings
    videoStartFrame -> gfx_start_frame
  mainTick()          game              the tick, the AI, the display-list build
    rdpCreateTask -> videoSubmitCommands -> gfx_run()
                      gfxdl             gfx_run_dl + the final flush
                      gfxend            end_frame + the pre-swap callback
                      pace              the CADisplayLink wait - this is SLACK
                      swap              eglSwapBuffers through ANGLE-Metal
  schedEndFrame()     sched             input, the per-frame ticks, the audio push
    videoEndFrame -> gfx_end_frame
                      finish            finish_render() - the GPU fence

plus two nested rows: `tex` (import_texture, inside gfxdl) and `xbla` (an STFS
read + LZX inflate + untile, inside tex). import_texture() is wrapped rather
than instrumented in place because it returns from several points; the XBLA
decode is wrapped at its five call sites for the same reason.

`pace` is the row to read first. It is not a cost - it is what the frame had
left over. It goes to zero exactly when the game stops making the rate.

